sequenceDiagram
    participant User as Data Scientist
    participant Dashboard as odh-dashboard
    participant KServe as KServe Controller
    participant LLMIS as LLMInferenceService<br/>Controller
    participant ODHModel as odh-model-controller
    participant Router as llm-d Router (EPP)
    participant WVA as Workload Variant<br/>Autoscaler
    participant Gateway as Platform Gateway<br/>(Envoy + kube-auth-proxy)
    participant AuthProxy as kube-auth-proxy
    participant Authorino as Kuadrant AuthPolicy<br/>(Authorino)
    participant ModelSvc as vLLM / Model Server
    participant S3 as S3 Storage
    participant Client as External API Client

    Note over User,Client: Workflow 1: LLM Model Serving (LLMInferenceService)

    User->>Gateway: Login via OAuth2/OIDC
    Gateway->>AuthProxy: ext_authz validation
    AuthProxy-->>Gateway: Auth OK + user identity
    Gateway-->>User: Authenticated session

    User->>Dashboard: Create LLMInferenceService<br/>(model, runtime, hardware profile)
    Dashboard->>KServe: Create LLMInferenceService CR<br/>(K8s API)

    LLMIS->>LLMIS: Reconcile LLMInferenceService
    Note over LLMIS: Creates LeaderWorkerSet,<br/>Gateway API HTTPRoute,<br/>GIE InferencePool,<br/>DRA ResourceClaimTemplate,<br/>PodMonitor, VariantAutoscaling

    ODHModel->>ODHModel: Watch LLMInferenceService
    Note over ODHModel: Creates Kuadrant AuthPolicy<br/>on HTTPRoute, injects<br/>HardwareProfile constraints

    KServe->>ModelSvc: Mutating webhook intercepts pod<br/>Injects: storage initializer,<br/>agent sidecar, metrics aggregator
    ModelSvc->>S3: Download model artifacts<br/>(HTTPS/443, AWS IAM)
    S3-->>ModelSvc: Model weights + config

    Note over ModelSvc: Model loaded, server ready

    WVA->>ModelSvc: Monitor GPU saturation<br/>and KV cache utilization
    Note over WVA: Queueing theory-based<br/>replica scaling

    Client->>Gateway: POST /v1/chat/completions<br/>(HTTPS/443, TLS 1.3)
    Gateway->>Authorino: AuthPolicy check<br/>(bearer/API key/anonymous)
    Authorino-->>Gateway: Authorized
    Gateway->>Router: ext_proc gRPC/9002<br/>Endpoint selection request
    Router->>Router: Load-aware, prefix-cache-aware<br/>endpoint selection
    Router-->>Gateway: Selected backend pod
    Gateway->>ModelSvc: Forward to selected pod<br/>(HTTP/8000)
    ModelSvc-->>Gateway: Inference response
    Gateway-->>Client: JSON response<br/>(HTTPS/443)

sequenceDiagram
    participant User as Data Scientist
    participant Dashboard as odh-dashboard
    participant DSPApi as DSP API Server
    participant ArgoCtrl as Argo Workflows<br/>Controller
    participant Launcher as DSP Launcher<br/>(sidecar)
    participant MLMD as ML Metadata<br/>gRPC Server
    participant PersAgent as DSP Persistence<br/>Agent
    participant S3 as S3 Storage
    participant KServe as KServe
    participant ModelReg as Model Registry

    Note over User,ModelReg: Workflow 2: ML Pipeline Execution

    User->>Dashboard: Navigate to Pipelines UI
    Dashboard->>DSPApi: List pipelines<br/>(REST/8080, service-ca TLS)

    User->>Dashboard: Trigger pipeline run
    Dashboard->>DSPApi: Create pipeline run<br/>(REST/8080)

    DSPApi->>DSPApi: Validate pipeline spec,<br/>store metadata in MariaDB
    DSPApi->>ArgoCtrl: Create Argo Workflow CR

    ArgoCtrl->>ArgoCtrl: Orchestrate DAG execution
    Note over ArgoCtrl: Creates pods for each<br/>pipeline step with driver<br/>and launcher sidecars

    loop Each pipeline step
        Launcher->>S3: Download input artifacts<br/>(HTTPS/443, IAM)
        Note over Launcher: Execute user container
        Launcher->>S3: Upload output artifacts<br/>(HTTPS/443, IAM)
        Launcher->>MLMD: Publish execution metadata<br/>(gRPC/8887)
    end

    PersAgent->>ArgoCtrl: Watch Workflow status
    PersAgent->>DSPApi: Sync run state<br/>(gRPC)

    Note over Launcher: Final step: model training complete

    Launcher->>ModelReg: Register trained model<br/>(REST/8080, metadata + S3 path)
    Launcher->>KServe: Create InferenceService CR<br/>(auto-deploy to serving)

    KServe->>S3: Download model artifacts
    Note over KServe: Model deployed and serving

sequenceDiagram
    participant User as Data Scientist
    participant SDK as Kubeflow SDK /<br/>Training Hub
    participant Trainer as Kubeflow Trainer
    participant Kueue as Kueue
    participant Workers as Training Runtime Pods<br/>(PyTorch DDP / DeepSpeed)
    participant Ray as KubeRay Cluster
    participant MLflow as MLflow
    participant ModelReg as Model Registry
    participant KServe as KServe
    participant S3 as S3 Storage

    Note over User,S3: Workflow 3: Distributed Training Job

    User->>SDK: Submit TrainJob CR<br/>(framework, model, dataset,<br/>resource requirements)
    SDK->>Trainer: Create TrainJob CR

    Trainer->>Trainer: Reconcile TrainJob:<br/>resolve ClusterTrainingRuntime,<br/>create JobSet with worker pods
    Trainer->>Kueue: Submit workload with<br/>WorkloadPriorityClass labels

    Kueue->>Kueue: Admit workload based on<br/>ClusterQueue quotas and<br/>resource availability
    Kueue-->>Workers: Schedule pod placement

    Workers->>S3: Download training dataset<br/>(HTTPS/443, IAM)

    Note over Workers: Execute distributed training<br/>PyTorch DDP / DeepSpeed / MPI

    opt Ray-based training
        Workers->>Ray: CodeFlare SDK manages<br/>RayCluster for distributed compute
    end

    loop Training epochs
        Workers->>MLflow: Log metrics, checkpoints,<br/>hyperparameters<br/>(REST/5000)
        Workers->>S3: Save model checkpoints<br/>(HTTPS/443, IAM)
    end

    Note over Workers: Training complete

    Workers->>ModelReg: Register trained model<br/>(REST/8080, version metadata,<br/>serving config, lineage)
    ModelReg->>S3: Store artifact reference

    User->>KServe: Deploy model for serving
    KServe->>ModelReg: Fetch model location
    KServe->>S3: Download model artifacts
    Note over KServe: Model serving via<br/>InferenceService

sequenceDiagram
    participant User as Data Scientist
    participant Dashboard as odh-dashboard
    participant EvalHub as EvalHub
    participant TrustyAIOp as TrustyAI Service<br/>Operator (LMES)
    participant LMEval as LM Evaluation<br/>Harness
    participant ModelSvc as KServe<br/>InferenceService
    participant TrustyAISvc as TrustyAI Service
    participant Prometheus as Prometheus
    participant GORCH as GORCH Orchestrator
    participant NeMo as NeMo Guardrails
    participant Detectors as Guardrails Detectors

    Note over User,Detectors: Workflow 4: Model Evaluation and Guardrails

    User->>Dashboard: Initiate model evaluation
    Dashboard->>EvalHub: Create evaluation request<br/>(REST/8080, model endpoint,<br/>evaluation tasks)

    EvalHub->>TrustyAIOp: Create LMEvalJob CR<br/>(tenant namespace, Kueue scheduling)

    TrustyAIOp->>TrustyAIOp: Reconcile LMEvalJob:<br/>create K8s Job with<br/>lm-evaluation-harness container,<br/>inject kube-rbac-proxy sidecar

    LMEval->>ModelSvc: Execute evaluation benchmarks<br/>(HTTP/8080 inference requests)
    ModelSvc-->>LMEval: Inference responses
    LMEval-->>EvalHub: Evaluation results<br/>(REST/8080)

    EvalHub-->>Dashboard: Display evaluation metrics

    Note over TrustyAISvc,Prometheus: Continuous Fairness Monitoring

    TrustyAISvc->>ModelSvc: Monitor InferenceServices<br/>(watch CRs + inference data)
    TrustyAISvc->>TrustyAISvc: Compute fairness metrics<br/>(SPD, DIR), drift detection,<br/>bias tracking
    TrustyAISvc->>Prometheus: Export fairness metrics<br/>(HTTP/8080 metrics endpoint)

    Note over GORCH,Detectors: Inference-time Guardrails

    User->>GORCH: Inference request with<br/>guardrails enabled<br/>(HTTP/8000)
    GORCH->>Detectors: Pre-response safety check<br/>(regex PII, HuggingFace classifiers)
    Detectors-->>GORCH: Safety assessment
    GORCH->>ModelSvc: Forward to model<br/>(HTTP/8000)
    ModelSvc-->>GORCH: Model response
    GORCH->>Detectors: Post-response safety check<br/>(LLM-as-judge)
    Detectors-->>GORCH: Safety assessment
    GORCH-->>User: Filtered response
